## P2-1: Manual Testing Checklist

**Status**: Not Started
**Effort**: Small (1 hour)
**Dependencies**: All P0 and P1 items
**Spec Reference**: README.md (How to Use, Accessibility) • **Status Reference**: STATUS-2025-12-07-230442.md recommendations

### Description
Create and execute a comprehensive manual testing checklist for all fixed animation files.

### Testing Checklist

For each fixed file, verify:

**Initial State:**
- [ ] Page loads with blank/waiting state (no animation playing)

**Entrance Animation:**
- [ ] Click triggers entrance animation
- [ ] Entrance animation plays smoothly
- [ ] Entrance completes within expected duration

**Hold State:**
- [ ] After entrance, animation enters hold state
- [ ] Hold state persists for ~2 seconds
- [ ] Visual feedback during hold (completed animation visible)

**Exit Animation (Auto-triggered):**
- [ ] After hold timeout, exit animation starts automatically
- [ ] Exit animation plays smoothly
- [ ] Exit animation completes within expected duration

**Waiting State:**
- [ ] After exit completes, animation STOPS (does not restart)
- [ ] Page returns to waiting state
- [ ] No infinite loop or auto-restart behavior

**User Interactions:**
- [ ] Click during waiting state restarts animation (entrance)
- [ ] Click during entrance state restarts animation from beginning
- [ ] Click during hold state triggers exit animation immediately
- [ ] Click during exit state has defined behavior (restart or no-op)

**PostMessage Restart:**
- [ ] PostMessage event triggers restart from waiting state
- [ ] PostMessage event triggers restart from other states
- [ ] Animation responds correctly to new message content (if applicable)

**Accessibility:**
- [ ] `prefers-reduced-motion` is respected
- [ ] No flashing/strobing effects that could trigger issues
- [ ] Keyboard accessibility (if applicable)

### Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] All P0 files pass complete testing checklist
- [ ] All P1 files pass complete testing checklist
- [ ] Any failures documented and added to backlog

### Technical Notes
- Test in Chrome, Firefox, and Safari if possible
- Use browser dev tools to simulate `prefers-reduced-motion`
- Document any cross-browser inconsistencies

